    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Radix Ipecacoanhoe used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 305"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The young, tender, blanché shoots are boiled as a pot-herb, the pulp of the black berries is used to adulterate wine, and the root is an emetic, approaching nearly to Ipecacuanha."@en ;
